  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. **The Lead**: Player with 3♦ must play it (as a single or in a combo). 2. **Climbing**: Each player in turn must play a combination of the same type (single, pair, triple, or 5-card hand) that is higher in rank than the previous play. 3. **Ranks**: 2 (High) > A > K > Q ... > 3 (Low). 4. **Suits**: Spades > Hearts > Clubs > Diamonds (used to break ties in same-rank plays). 5. **Passing**: A player can pass at any time. When 3 players pass, the last player to play starts a new trick with any combo.',
    Player: '1. **The Lead**: Player with 3♦ must play it (as a single or in a combo). 2. **Climbing**: Each player in turn must play a combination of the same type (single, pair, triple, or 5-card hand) that is higher in rank than the previous play. 3. **Ranks**: 2 (High) > A > K > Q ... > 3 (Low). 4. **Suits**: Spades > Hearts > Clubs > Diamonds (used to break ties in same-rank plays). 5. **Passing**: A player can pass at any time. When 3 players pass, the last player to play starts a new trick with any combo.',
    objective: 'Be the first player to shed all cards from your hand.',
    gameplay: '1. **The Lead**: Player with 3♦ must play it (as a single or in a combo). 2. **Climbing**: Each player in turn must play a combination of the same type (single, pair, triple, or 5-card hand) that is higher in rank than the previous play. 3. **Ranks**: 2 (High) > A > K > Q ... > 3 (Low). 4. **Suits**: Spades > Hearts > Clubs > Diamonds (used to break ties in same-rank plays). 5. **Passing**: A player can pass at any time. When 3 players pass, the last player to play starts a new trick with any combo.',
    keyRules: [
      '5-card combinations must follow poker rankings: Royal Flush > Straight Flush > 4-of-a-Kind > Full House > Flush > Straight.',
      'The rank of a 5-card combo is determined by its highest card (e.g., an Ace-high Flush beats a King-high Flush).',
      'If you pass, you can still play later in the same trick cycle if the lead has not been reset.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Typically 4 players playing individually.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck (No Jokers).',
      equipment: 'Standard pack, score pad.',
      dealing: 'Deal the entire deck clockwise (13 cards to each player). The player holding the 3 of Diamonds leads the first trick.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. **The Lead**: Player with 3♦ must play it (as a single or in a combo). 2. **Climbing**: Each player in turn must play a combination of the same type (single, pair, triple, or 5-card hand) that is higher in rank than the previous play. 3. **Ranks**: 2 (High) > A > K > Q ... > 3 (Low). 4. **Suits**: Spades > Hearts > Clubs > Diamonds (used to break ties in same-rank plays). 5. **Passing**: A player can pass at any time. When 3 players pass, the last player to play starts a new trick with any combo.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Big Two is a point-based shedding game played without a pre-hand monetary ante.',
      deal: 'The entire 52-card deck is distributed equally by the system dealer at the start of the round.',
      reveal_market: 'This is a closed-hand climbing game where all cards are held privately; no community market exists.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap cards from any external area; they must succeed with their initial 13 cards.',
      buy_stock: 'The entire deck is distributed at once; no cards remain in stock to be purchased during play.',
      fold: 'Players must remain in the game until a winner has shed all cards to determine the penalty counts.',
      check: 'The game uses a climbing and passing structure rather than a vying structure with checks and bets.',
      call: 'There is no pot or bet to match in Big Two; competition is based on combination rankings.',
      bet: 'The game is scored via penalty points for cards remaining in hand rather than through wagering.',
      raise: 'There are no wagering rounds in this game, so the value of the deal cannot be increased via raises.',
      declare: 'Winning results are immediate upon playing the last card; no formal declaration phase is required.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands remain private until individual cards are played into climbing combos; no showdown occurs.',
      award_pot: 'Points are tallied on a scorecard after each hand; there is no physical pot of assets to award.',
      play_card: 'Must match the combination type and exceed the previous rank/suit.',
      draw: 'Each player receives thirteen cards at the start and no further drawing occurs during the play phase.',
      discard: 'Every card must be shed through valid climbing combinations; there is no separate discard or waste pile.',
      pass: 'Allowed at any time during the climbing phase.',
      bid: 'Big Two does not utilize a bidding system to determine the dealer, trump, or game objectives.',
      meld: 'This is a climbing game based on beating combinations rather than creating or laying down melds.',
      go_out: 'A player wins the round automatically upon playing their final combination from hand.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 13 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first player to shed all cards from your hand.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. **The Lead**: Player with 3♦ must play it (as a single or in a combo). 2. **Climbing**: Each player in turn must play a combination of the same type (single, pair, triple, or 5-card hand) that is higher in rank than the previous play. 3. **Ranks**: 2 (High) > A > K > Q ... > 3 (Low). 4. **Suits**: Spades > Hearts > Clubs > Diamonds (used to break ties in same-rank plays). 5. **Passing**: A player can pass at any time. When 3 players pass, the last player to play starts a new trick with any combo.',
      'Scoring example: Losers receive penalty points based on remaining cards (1x, 2x, or 3x multipliers). First player to empty their hand wins the round..',
